The implementation now removes the second synchronization and cuts the successful path to:

- one selected-worktree validation;
- one full refresh after the integration commit;
- selected-record-only refresh when parking;
- no status refresh after deleting the already-unchecked-out branch.

I’ve added assertions for exactly one full read/one target revalidation during integration, and zero full reads during park/delete cleanup.

